.PP
\f[CR]decode\f[R] reads a \f[CR]std::vector\f[R] or a
\f[CR]std::array\f[R] of a number type only from its typed array.
A plain array of numbers gives \f[CR]incorrect_type\f[R].
.PP
An enum needs a fixed underlying type, for example
\f[CR]enum class color : std::uint8_t { red, green };\f[R].
Without it, \f[CR]decode\f[R] does not compile.
.SS 3. Keys
The key of a member is its name.
A description changes it.
\f[CR]CBOR_DEFINE_TYPE(type, tag, members...)\f[R] writes the
description at global scope, after the struct: the tag of the struct and
one entry for each public member.
The tag is a \f[CR]cbor::tag{n}\f[R], or \f[CR]cbor::untagged\f[R] for a
map with no tag.
The entry \f[CR]cbor::member{key, &type::member}\f[R] gives the key.
A key is a text or an integer.
\f[CR]CBOR_MEMBER(type, member)\f[R] takes the name as the key.
\f[CR]CBOR_DEFINE_TYPE_MEMBERS(type, tag, names...)\f[R] takes the names
only, and each name is its key.
The macro writes a specialization of \f[CR]cbor::describe_members\f[R],
which cbor::schema reads too.
An annotation \f[CR][[=cbor::key(\(dqx\(dq)]]\f[R] or
\f[CR][[=cbor::tag(n)]]\f[R] on a type that \f[CR]structs\f[R] reads
does not compile.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]struct\f[R] header {
    std::string content_type;
};

CBOR_DEFINE_TYPE(header, cbor::tag{160060}, cbor::member{\(dqcontent\-type\(dq, &header::content_type});

\f[I]// header{\(dqtext/plain\(dq} is 160060({\(dqcontent\-type\(dq: \(dqtext/plain\(dq})\f[R]
.EE
.PP
A struct whose description has a tag carries that tag.
\f[CR]decode\f[R] gives \f[CR]incorrect_type\f[R] when the tag is
missing or is another tag.
.PP
\f[CR]encode\f[R] leaves out a \f[CR]std::optional\f[R] member that is
empty.
\f[CR]decode\f[R] gives an empty \f[CR]std::optional\f[R] when its key
is not in the map.
.SS 4. Input from other programs
\f[CR]decode\f[R] reads the keys of a map in any order and skips a key
that no member has.
So a program reads the bytes of a newer program that added members.
A new member of type \f[CR]std::optional\f[R] also reads the bytes of an
older program.
.PP
